# Copy this file to .env in the repo root and fill in your key.
# .env is gitignored: never commit it.
# Format: one NAME=value per line. No quotes, no spaces around "=", no "export".
# `make check` and every test run on a scripted fake model and need no key.

# Required: `make run` and every eval target use your OpenCode Go subscription
# (runtime glm-5.3-flash, judge kimi-k3.1-pro). Paste the API key from opencode.ai/auth.
OPENCODE_API_KEY=
# The runtime model: glm-5.3-flash (the default) or glm-5.3; no other is accepted.
# MERIDIAN_RUNTIME_MODEL=glm-5.3

# Optional: run the assistant (`make run`) on Groq GPT-OSS 120B instead, the runtime that
# eval/REPORT.md measured. Needs a Groq API key ("gsk_..."); then remove the "# " below.
GROQ_API_KEY=
# MERIDIAN_RUNTIME_PROVIDER=groq

# Optional. The header value for reading a ticket back in the demo.
# MERIDIAN_STAFF_KEY=dev-staff-key
